        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a typical water-based asphalt sealer in good weather, expect a few hours to walk on it, roughly four to eight hours before a second coat, and about 24 to 48 hours before driving on it. Cool temperatures, humidity, shade, and heavy coats all push those numbers out, sometimes by a day or more.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use the label as a minimum, check the shadiest and lowest spots before trusting the whole driveway, and take it easy on the surface for the first week. An extra day of parking on the street is a far smaller cost than tire marks that last until the next reseal.
          </p>
